{
  "about": "clef is a Cloudflare Workers AI model, so from 0.2.0 its errors map by the Workers AI code in the reply first, and by HTTP status only for a code the shared table does not list. Each clef row shows the code, its class, whether it is stored, and whether it stops the call; was is the code the 0.1.0 status-only mapping gave the same reply, where it differs. account_limit_exhausted and account_not_entitled are batch-level: never stored, they stop the call, and on the call's first provider call they refuse the whole call at admission (first_call_refusals). TypeSafe documents no error codes, and its mapping is unchanged.",
